module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.cumulative_metric_read_as_per_event

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data cumulative_metric_read_as_per_event: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "cumulative_metric_read_as_per_event" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "a metric that ACCOUNTS is read as a metric that MEASURES (an upstream counter or histogram whose observation is booked once per request, per retention decision or per accounting event, consumed as though it described one event, one step or one instant; the arithmetic succeeds, the units look right, and the answer is about a different quantity).",
    "RECOGNITION: the reading is plausible, dimensionally consistent, and nobody can name the line of upstream source that defines the observation. Ask what the producer OBSERVES, not what the name suggests, and ask it of the installed binary rather than the upstream repository — a self-reported version string is a claim the process makes about itself, not executable provenance.",
    "WHY IT RECURS: these metrics are the only cheap window into a closed upstream, so a wrong reading is not caught by the substrate at all — it is caught by a prediction failing in production, weeks later, against a number that looked authoritative on a dashboard. Two independent investigators reached the SAME wrong root cause from the same histogram in one afternoon, which is the tell that the metric's name was doing the reasoning.",
    "RECEIPTS 2026-09-06/07, DeepSeek V4 Flash on the Spark pairs. (1) kv_cache_usage_perc read as occupancy: it counts every block that is not FREE and an evictable cached prefix is not free, so a warm idle engine reads ~99%; the dashboard rendered it red and captioned it 'referenced by running requests' beside REQ 0, and the router's load-aware landing classified every replica as saturated and silently degraded to the load-blind path it was written to replace — live and inert for a day while one head took all traffic and the other took none.",
    "(2) iteration_tokens_total read as tokens-computed-per-engine-step: the build observes `prompt_token_stats.total`, the FULL prompt length of each prefill booked in one iteration, plus generation tokens. Its large buckets therefore count large-PROMPT REQUESTS, not stop-the-world steps. A single observation of 247,582 tokens was read as one monolithic engine step and produced a confident root cause.",
    "(3) Ethernet netdev rx_bytes/tx_bytes read as interconnect traffic: the ranks speak RoCE, whose bytes never reach those counters, so a 176-second prefill measured as ~0 GB of inter-node traffic. The same prefill moved 175 GB per rank on the RoCE port counters. An earlier reading of that port taken across a CACHE HIT was then reported as prefill utilisation.",
    "(4) THE SHARPEST INSTANCE, AND IT CORRECTED ITSELF ONCE IN THE WRONG DIRECTION BEFORE IT WAS SETTLED. iteration_tokens_total_count is ENGINE-WIDE, so a co-tenant's output batches land in any window measured around one probe. Dividing a request's computed tokens by that count produced 158,764 / 83 = ~1,913 tokens, which was read as the effective scheduler budget and matched to vLLM's 2048 fallback; three further conclusions were built on it. That reading was then WITHDRAWN on the ground that the same counter, polled on an idle engine, showed every window from 512 to 20,082 computed tokens completing in exactly ONE iteration — so the budget was declared to be at least 20,082, an order of magnitude higher, and the 2048 was declared refuted.",
    "THE WITHDRAWAL WAS THE SECOND INSTANCE OF THE SAME MODE, AND EXCLUSIVITY IS WHAT MADE IT LOOK SAFE. The remedy adopted at the time — measure on an idle engine, where no other request increments the count, so the engine-wide count IS the per-request step count — is FALSE, and it is false for a reason no amount of exclusivity repairs: the counter does not count steps on any engine. vllm/v1/engine/async_llm.py builds the stats object as `IterationStats() if (log_stats and num_outputs) else None` and the recorder returns early on None, so it advances once per EngineCoreOutputs batch CARRYING AN OUTPUT. A chunked-prefill step emits no output for the request it is advancing, so a prefill-only request advances the count EXACTLY ONCE however many chunks it ran. The observation 'one iteration' was therefore invariant across the whole sweep and carried no information about the budget at all — it would read 1 for 512 tokens and for 512,000. Measured 2026-09-07 across a batch-budget sweep: requests that a true per-step counter measured at 3, 4, 7, 9 and 10 steps each advanced this count by 1.",
    "(5) THE NEAR MISS IS THE SPECIMEN, NOT THE ERROR. 1,913 was not a fabricated quantity that coincidentally resembled 2048. A co-tenant decoder beside a chunked prefill receives exactly one token per chunk — because chunked prefill runs as a MIXED batch — and each of those tokens is one output batch, so the engine-wide count advances once per chunk and the quotient approximates the chunk size BY CONSTRUCTION. 158,764 / 2048 = 77.5 chunks against 83 observed advances, and the 2.30s median interval is one 2048-token step. The original inference reached the right answer through a mechanism nobody had identified, was accepted for the wrong reason, and was then discarded for a worse one. THE STANDING LESSON: a wrong-grain quotient can land NEAR the true answer, and the near-miss is exactly what makes it unfalsifiable by inspection — first as apparent confirmation, then as apparent refutation. Neither the agreement nor the disagreement of a wrong-grain quantity with an independent fact is evidence about either.",
    "THE SETTLED READING, established by three instruments that do not share the defect. FIRST, a true per-step counter: under --enable-mfu-metrics, vllm:estimated_flops_per_gpu_total advances once per engine step in a fixed quantum, and its step counts came out as exactly ceil(tokens / 2048) at seven probe sizes. SECOND, the engine's own emitted configuration: the startup banner logs compile_ranges_endpoints [2048], and vllm/config/vllm.py::_set_compile_ranges sets that endpoint FROM scheduler_config.max_num_batched_tokens. THIRD, a victim-side behavioural ceiling: vllm:inter_token_latency_seconds over a 45-hour launch held 1,454,342 samples with one above 5s and none above 7.5s, which alone refutes a 20,082-token step (~21s). The effective budget is 2048, and it was selected by an absorbing fallback in upstream's device-memory probe rather than by anyone's decision — filed at gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.absorbing_fallback.",
    "THE STANDING REMEDY IS NOW THREE WALLS, BECAUSE ATTRIBUTION AND GRAIN WERE NECESSARY AND NOT SUFFICIENT. FIRST, ATTRIBUTION: an aggregate delta belongs to one request only under a complete attribution boundary — same launch throughout, exact start and end, no counter reset, complete label population, no foreign contributor, and no booking that lands outside the window. Sparse polling earns only NO FOREIGN REQUEST OBSERVED AT THIS POLLING GRAIN, which is weaker than exclusivity and must be named as such.",
    "SECOND, GRAIN: even under perfect attribution, dividing a delta by an event count yields a POPULATION MEAN and nothing else — not any particular event's size, not the maximum, not the distribution, not a configured limit. An exact per-event quantity requires either a ONE-EVENT population or per-event accounting emitted by the producer.",
    "THIRD, AND THIS IS WHAT THE WITHDRAWAL MISSED: THE COUNTER'S ADVANCE CONDITION IS ITSELF A FACT TO BE READ, NOT INFERRED FROM ITS NAME OR ITS BEHAVIOUR UNDER A CONVENIENT SETUP. Before a count is used as a population size, name the line in the INSTALLED source that decides when it advances, and state which events it skips. Exclusivity answers WHOSE events are counted; it says nothing about WHICH events are counted, and a counter that skips the very events under study is not repaired by removing other tenants. The discriminating check is cheap and was available the whole time: a reading that stays CONSTANT while the subject varies over a wide range is measuring something else, and 'one iteration' across a 39x token range was that reading.",
    "SHAPE, AND WHY IT IS ONE MODE RATHER THAN FIVE: each is a cumulative accounting quantity consumed as an instantaneous or per-event one. The remedy is the same in all of them — bind the reading to what the producer observes, at the revision and binary that produced it, and make the wrong question refuse rather than return a number. That refusal now exists as extdeps.vllm.metrics, which pairs a metric with a QUESTION and refuses the pairings the source does not support, including this one.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
